# Architecture

Local code-change board (not deployments/runtime ops). Talks to forges via CLIs on the machine.

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| GitHub | `gh` |
| GitLab | `glab` |
| Auth | Existing CLI login sessions |
| AI triage | Optional OpenAI-compatible chat in config `llm` |
| Agent sessions | `strop/agentsession` (prune investigate) via published module |
| Supervision | process-compose (`make serve`); `gitboard serve` for one-off |

## Packages

```
cmd/gitboard/           # CLI: init, sync, serve
internal/config/        # XDG config load/save
internal/cliexec/       # shared gh/glab/git exec
internal/board/         # shared JSON data types (DTOs) for dashboard UI and forge adapters
internal/remotegit/     # GitHub + GitLab adapters (uses board for shared types)
internal/localgit/      # checkouts, worktrees, pull ff-only
internal/syncproj/      # discover + select tracked projects
internal/dashboard/     # aggregate rows for UI; Service (read) and Commands (write) types
internal/server/        # HTTP + static UI
internal/server/static/ # dashboard assets
internal/triage/        # AI failure triage
internal/llm/           # OpenAI-compatible client
internal/pruneagent/    # investigate removable branches
internal/observability/ # OTEL hooks
```

**Dependency direction:** `cmd` → `internal/*`; domain packages must not import `cmd`. Prefer `cliexec` for process calls. Do not grow business logic in `main` switch arms beyond flag parse + wire-up.

## strop dependency

`go.mod` requires the published module (`github.com/behaviorengineering/strop vX.Y.Z`). No git submodule.

**Bump a release:** `go get github.com/behaviorengineering/strop@vX.Y.Z` then `go mod tidy`.

**Local strop changes (rare):** develop in a sibling clone, temporarily add it to root `go.work`, then release strop and bump the require. Do not commit a long-lived `replace` or re-add a submodule unless the user asks.

```
# sibling layout example
use (
	.
	../strop
)
```

After the strop PR/tag lands: remove the sibling `use` line (keep `go.work` with `.` only), `go get …@vX.Y.Z`, `go mod tidy`.

## Dashboard behavior

- Project list order (UI): attention first (failed CI, conflicts, open review, dirty, prune hint, behind-only vs origin on a real pull candidate), then A–Z by label. Behind attention matches the pull affordance: detached pins (common for submodules) and their unrelated `origin_sync` branch rows do not count. Active search keeps relevance first, then the same attention / A–Z tiebreak. Config `projects` order is not the board order.
- **Views:** config `views` are named subsets of tracked project ids (membership may overlap). `GET /api/dashboard?view=<id>` forge-loads only that subset. Empty/omitted `views` synthesizes an implicit `default` view over all projects. The UI switcher persists the active view in localStorage. Switching a view selects the tab immediately, shows a busy spinner on that tab while the fetch runs (dimmer fill while loading, brighter active fill when done), paints a per-view cache instantly when available, then refreshes in the background. There is no “load everything” control in v1.
- Branches column: remote heads from the forge (up to 20); default + open PR/MR first, then by recency. Each row has its own latest CI. CI-only refs do not invent branch rows. Empty `ui.hide_branches` shows all; `path.Match` patterns hide matching names from the board only (forge prune data unchanged), including UI “local only” rows synthesized from local checkouts. After hide, `open_items` and the Open review chip / attention rank count only still-visible `open_review` branches.
- Local status beside each remote branch (checked out, dirty, ↑/↓ vs origin). Ahead/behind uses `git fetch --prune origin` (TTL: `local.fetch_seconds`, default 120; `?fresh=1` bypasses) then compares local heads to `origin/<branch>`. Behind + clean → **pull** is ff-only (`git pull --ff-only`, or `git fetch origin branch:branch` when not checked out), then `git submodule update --init --recursive` on the checked-out worktree so nested pins (for example `.cursor/packs/shared`) match the new tip. Stale submodule checkouts that only look dirty are synced before pull refuses a dirty tree. Each local appearance (checkout/submodule) with behind-only + clean also gets its own pull control; pulls start immediately (no confirm) and may run in parallel. If `index.lock` is older than 30s, pull and safe-remove return HTTP 409 `stale_index_lock` so the UI can ask to remove the lock and retry with `clear_index_lock`; a fresher lock is refused (another git process may still be running). **Prune hints** (remote head gone + clean + no open PR/MR): **safe** when the forge has a merged PR/MR for that branch name (recent merged list or a per-branch lookup), or local tip content already matches default (`origin/<default>` preferred; ancestor or identical trees, covering squash merges). **likely** only after a per-branch merged lookup confirms there is no matching PR/MR; a missing page of recent merges is not enough. Missing forge data shows no hint. A branch still listed in the UI Branches column (or with an open review) never gets a prune hint, even if content-on-default would otherwise say safe. Investigate uses the same content-on-default check so unique SHAs alone do not force keep after squash. **Safe prune** on the main worktree updates the default branch from origin before switching onto it and deleting the merged branch (ff-only when possible; if default is not checked out and has diverged, the local default tip is moved to `origin/<default>`, discarding local-only commits on that tip). Worktrees with no remote head are “local only”. Detached HEAD that matches a tag exactly shows the tag name (SHA in tooltip), not only `detached <sha>`. Submodule worktree paths resolve to the checkout (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`), not the `.git/modules` git dir.
- `gitboard sync` and the board **Manage** UI write config; a running `serve` reloads the full config file when its mtime advances and clears the forge + origin-fetch TTL caches when the tracked project set, view membership, or `local.roots` changes (no restart required for add/remove, views, roots, or `ui.hide_branches` edits). Manage **Tracked** lists projects under host subtabs (GitHub, GitLab, …) sorted A–Z by label within the active host; **Discover**, **Views**, **Local**, and **Sources** cover the rest of sync config.

## HTTP API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `GET` | `/api/health` | Liveness |
| `GET` | `/api/meta` | Server meta (`poll_interval_seconds`, `ui.hide_branches`, `views`) |
| `GET` | `/api/dashboard` | Aggregated rows for one view (`?view=` required for non-default; `?fresh=1` forces refresh); includes `ui`, `views`, `active_view` |
| `GET` | `/api/failures?project=&run_id=` | Failed jobs |
| `POST` | `/api/triage` | AI log analysis |
| `POST` | `/api/prune/safe` | Re-check hints; remove a safe local checkout (`clear_index_lock` after 409 `stale_index_lock`) |
| `POST` | `/api/pull/ff` | Fast-forward local branch from origin (ff-only; same `clear_index_lock` confirm) |
| `POST` | `/api/local/sync/investigate` | Refresh origin and compare local branch commits |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/prune/investigate` | Likely-removable branch evidence + session card |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/sessions/:id` | Session meta, card, turns |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/sessions/:id/failure` | Failure dump when present |
| `GET` | `/api/sync/candidates` | Discover forge repos from `sync` sources (`?host=`); JSON `candidates` plus optional `warnings` for per-source forge failures |
| `POST` | `/api/sync/projects` | Add, remove, or set `local_path` on a tracked project (`action` add/remove/set_local_path) |
| `PUT` | `/api/sync/selection` | Replace tracked set from selected host/path refs |
| `GET`/`PUT` | `/api/sync/sources` | Read/update GitHub orgs and GitLab groups |
| `GET`/`PUT` | `/api/local/roots` | Read/update `local.roots` scan directories |
| `GET`/`PUT` | `/api/views` | Read sync state / replace named view definitions |

